        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. Starmer rival seeks win in UK by-election pivotal to prime minister's fate Europe Issued on: 18/06/2026 - 12:31 Modified: 18/06/2026 - 12:32 The UK's Prime Minister Keir Starmer has insisted he will fight to stay in his role if a leadership challenge is launched by Andy Burnham. But before any such contest unfolds, Burnham must win a seat in parliament, which he is hoping to do on June 18 in a by-election in the Makerfield constituency. The race is expected to be tight, with Reform UK candidate Rob Kenyon posing a credible opposition to the former Greater Manchester Mayor. Climate-change driven heatwave brings uncertainty to French farmers 18/06/2026 Europe Starmer on the line as UK holds \"most important local election in decades\" 18/06/2026 Europe US tells NATO it will review its force presence in Europe 18/06/2026 Europe Is football coming home? English fans tell FRANCE 24 18/06/2026 Europe G7 summit hailed a success by Macron thanks to developments on Ukraine and Iran 17/06/2026 Europe Replay: Macron holds press conference as G7 summit comes to an end 17/06/2026 Europe G7 focuses on AI's contentious future and US industry dominance 17/06/2026 Europe Trump doesn't rule out strikes on Iran despite agreement, looks to support Ukraine 17/06/2026 Middle East Despite agreement, G7 looks to decrease Strait of Hormuz reliance 17/06/2026 Europe"
